  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry with near normal temperatures through the week, \nfor pleasant fall weather.\n\nHigh pressure will remain over the region today, and through much of \nthe next week, with broad 500mb troughing over the eastern US. \nBreezy winds today will subside by this evening. With good \nradiational cooling conditions again tonight, will likely see \ntemperatures near to below freezing in the mountains and mid 30s in \nthe Piedmont. Will likely be some frost again tomorrow morning in \nthe mountains, so please continue taking any precautions to protect \nsensitive vegetation. Since the growing season has ended for zones \nwest of the Blue Ridge given the widespread freezing temperatures \nacross those areas, Frost and Freeze headlines will no longer be \nissued. The growing season remains open for the Piedmont and Roanoke \nValley at this time.\n\nWinds vary slightly from the northwest to northwest throughout the \nweek, and surface high pressure will continue to provide dry and \nclear weather. Temperatures will gradually moderate towards seasonal \nnormals after the start of the week, high temperatures in the 60s \nand 70s, and lows in the 30s and 40s.",
